<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila's PHIBOR rates mostly higher.</title>
<headline>Manila's PHIBOR rates mostly higher.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine interbank offered rates (PHIBOR) were mostly higher on Tuesday with only the one-year term steady, traders said.</p>
<p>PHIBOR rose in line with the increase in Treasury bill rates during the auction on Monday, they said.</p>
<p>Dealers said they expected interest rates to eventually move higher in line with the rise in wages and an expected increase in oil prices with the full deregulation of the oil industry.</p>
<p>PHIBOR represents rates at which banks would be willing to swap their pesos with dollars.  </p>
<p>Average rates quoted by 20 banks were:</p>
<p>			  FEB 4		 FEB 3</p>
<p>    1 W		9 15/16		 9  7/8</p>
<p>    2 W		9 15/16		 9 13/16</p>
<p>    1 M		10  1/8		 10</p>
<p>    2 M		10  3/16		10</p>
<p>    3 M		10  3/16		10  1/16</p>
<p>    6 M		10  1/4		 10  1/8</p>
<p>    12M		10  7/16		10  7/16</p>
<p>    VAL		5-Feb		   4-Feb</p>
<p>-- LILIAN KARUNUNGAN (632) 841-8937</p>
